Former Apple CFO Luca Maestri is taking another step back from the company, reports <em><a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-09-01/apple-s-former-cfo-maestri-drops-role-running-corporate-services">Bloomberg</a></em>. Maestri <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2024/08/26/apple-cfo-luca-maestri-stepping-down/">left his role</a> as CFO in January 2025, but stayed at Apple to run the company's Corporate Services teams.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2022/08/apple-cfo-luca-maestri.jpg" alt="" width="1172" height="682" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-859188" /><br/>
Maestri stepped down from that position in recent weeks, and <em>Bloomberg</em> says he is still at Apple but has no responsibilities other than hosting a class at Apple University. Maestri reported to former Apple CEO <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/tim-cook/">Tim Cook</a>, but he does not report to new Apple CEO John Ternus. Maestri is slowly withdrawing from Apple, and visits the office about once a week.<br/>
<br/>
Corporate services includes information systems and technology, information security, and real estate and development. The team is being taken over by Kevan Parekh, who became Apple's CFO after Maestri stepped down.<br/>
<br/>
